// DL-066a: indirect call through a function pointer (no malloc/heap) — locks
// down the fix for codegen-indirect-call-rb0-misuse. CALL_PSEUDO_INDIRECT used
// to expand to `CALL_RRII RB0, <target>, 0`, but rb0 as call base means "PC+4"
// (spec §1.3), not zero, so the computed target was PC+4+absolute_address.
// QEMU happened to run this "correctly" only because of the separate,
// unrelated QEMU-rb0-not-maintained defect (rb0 always reads 0 there); gem5
// correctly maintains rb0 and used to land at a garbage address before the fix.
// Dual-backend exit 42.
// RUN: %llvm-mc -triple=dadao -filetype=obj -o %t.crt0.o %S/../../scripts/crt0.s
// RUN: %clang --target=dadao-unknown-elf -nostdlib -Wl,-T,%S/../../scripts/dadao.ld %t.crt0.o %S/Inputs/indirect_call.c -o %t.elf
// RUN: %llvm-objcopy -O binary %t.elf %t.bin
// RUN: bash -c '%qemu -M dadao-m1 -nographic -bios %trampoline -kernel %t.bin >/dev/null 2>&1; test $? -eq 42'
// RUN: bash -c '%gem5 %gem5_se %t.elf >/dev/null 2>&1; test $? -eq 42'
